# Claude Code sandbox mask files. The bubblewrap sandbox protects shell, git
# and editor config by creating the path if missing and bind-mounting it
# read-only; a killed session leaves the 0-byte stub behind. None of these are
# ever tracked here (MCP servers are declared in workstation/agents/mcp-servers.nix,
# and flake inputs replace submodules), so ignoring them is safe. If one is ever
# wanted for real, `git add -f <path>`. Clean up stubs with `claude doctor`'s
# remedy while no session is running in this project.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.idea
/.mcp.json
/.profile
/.ripgreprc
/.vscode
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.claude/agents
